{"data": [{"author_id": "48463418", "created_at": "2026-10-27T19:43:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115167571204792565"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Despite many models proposed to explain charging behavior between insulating particles, the mechanisms underlying triboelectric charging have remained an open question in nonequilibrium physics. This manuscript presents a new experimental method to measure charge transfer during collisions between individual pairs of levitated particles, showing that charge evolution saturates as predicted by the condenser model.#AdvancingField #TimelyTopic #TheoryExperiment", "display_url": "go.aps.org/3UR62IH", "end": 221, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/3UR62IH", "images": [{"height": 200, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114642701505155072/nMliclBV?format=png&name=orig", "width": 200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114642701505155072/nMliclBV?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 198, "status": 200, "title": "It takes two to tribo: Stochastic charge evolution in repeated binary collisions of acoustically levitated particles", "unwound_url": "https://journals.aps.org/pre/abstract/10.1103/p9zp-hf26", "url": "https://t.co/KNX7pJ9OoK"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/bXDQejICCj", "end": 245, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/APSphysics/status/2115167571204792565/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115167568256274433", "start": 222, "url": "https://t.co/bXDQejICCj"}]}, "id": "2115167571204792565", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 771, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Two particles, levitated by sound, collide again and again. A study in Physical Review E tracks how electric charge builds up between them, a process called triboelectric charging.\n\nRead the study: https://t.co/KNX7pJ9OoK https://t.co/bXDQejICCj", "url": "https://x.com/APSphysics/status/2115167571204792565"}, {"author_id": "188369814", "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:17:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115145941347082405"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Ij3Sy2Wpma", "end": 271, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/biancoresearch/status/2115145941347082405/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115145838565498880", "start": 248, "url": "https://t.co/Ij3Sy2Wpma"}]}, "id": "2115145941347082405", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 18395, "like_count": 90, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 44, "retweet_count": 21}, "text": "What's going on with gas prices?\n\nSince gas prices are highly seasonal, it may help to look at them seasonally.\n\nThis chart shows prices each year (January 1st to December 31st) back to 2004.\n\nWe have never seen gas prices this high in the autumn. https://t.co/Ij3Sy2Wpma", "url": "https://x.com/biancoresearch/status/2115145941347082405"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:10:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115144166774858042"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/evilkaratesk8e…", "end": 229, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/evilkaratesk8er/status/2113854180263940408", "start": 206, "url": "https://t.co/BzMy3YmdIU"}]}, "id": "2115144166774858042", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 24150, "like_count": 207, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113854180263940408", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Avoiding negative polarization should be one of your main priorities in life. But I swear, some posts (and posters) are so unbelievably vapid, you come across them and start feel sympathetic to the YIMBYs. https://t.co/BzMy3YmdIU", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115144166774858042"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:03:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115142287592448098"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/_JoshSchafer/s…", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/_JoshSchafer/status/